    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d330">

                <pb facs="0309" n="299" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg299"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3–1449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-14T16:00:00+08:00">March 14, 1949—4
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 15—2:01 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>570. From Merchant. Ambassador concurs Sun and will take earliest opportunity
                    indicate to Acting President his confidence Sun’s qualifications. Sun due
                    Nanking within few days. Notwithstanding <pb facs="0310" n="300" xml:id="pg300"
                    /> angle reported Embtel 572, March 14,<anchor n="98" xml:id="d330-f1"/> I
                    believe prospect promising. I will return Taipei March 17 or 18 via Canton
                    (refDeptel 332, March 11). Pending clarification governorship, I do not
                    contemplate opening negotiation unless you instruct me to contrary.
                    [Merchant.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d330-f1" n="98" xml:id="d330-f1-content">
